# eteller

Workflow name is **eteller**. Do not name the workflow after the containing directory.

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), then `.memory/README.md` and `.memory/workflow.md`, then `workspace.config.md`.

## Layout

- `base/<REPO_DIR_NAME>/` — `INTEGRATION_BRANCH` only (coding law + campaign `.eteller/`)
- `waves/wave-N/<task-id>/<REPO_DIR_NAME>/` — one clone per wave-task branch
- Campaign docs live **inside** product clones under `.eteller/` (product branches), not on the eteller remote

## Coding law

Read **only** `base/<REPO_DIR_NAME>/CurrentTask/*AGENT_SPEC*.md` (read-only).
Do not treat wave-clone `CurrentTask/*AGENT_SPEC*` as law.

## Obligatory

- One agent = one task slot; product edits only in that clone cwd
- Skip slots with `state.md` `finished: true` / `status: closed`
- Subagents: `model: "cursor-grok-4.5-high"`
- Every wave-task has milestones in `.eteller/progress.md`; update on each milestone complete, then commit on the **wave-task branch**
- On complete: update `Reports/<task-id>.txt`, open PR to `INTEGRATION_BRANCH`, mark closed — **never auto-merge**
- Framework changes (`board/`, rules, `.memory/`, scripts, templates, README, example config): **commit and push** to eteller
- Never commit `base/` or `waves/` into eteller

## Prohibited

- Inventing `REPO_URL` / branches when `workspace.config.md` is empty
- Auto-merging PRs
- Implementing product features in the eteller framework tree
- Cross-slot edits
